▶️ FULL VIDEO: https://youtu.be/kpeTUPaUXu0
🎬 Wan Animate 2 vs Scail 2. Same seed, same footage, one winner.

Wan Animate 2 released on August 7th and everyone assumed it takes the crown for motion control in ComfyUI. I ran it head to head against Scail 2 on the same reference image, the same driving video, the same seed and the same resolution across three different clips. Animate 2 skips the pose skeleton entirely and feeds driving frames straight into the transformer, which sounds like a straight upgrade on paper. In practice it came back with discoloration on every single generation, shirt clipping and artifacting toward the end of the clips, while Scail 2 held color and kept the real background from the driving video.

Animate 2 did take one round on pure facial quality, and it generated in roughly half the time. It is going to be a monster once proper node support lands. Right now Scail 2 is still the one I'm using. Full breakdown, the workflow modifications, the LoRA stacks and all three side by side comparisons are in the full video.

